SIZE 35 mm, 25 mm
GAP 3 mm, 0 mm
DIRECTION 0,0
REFERENCE 0,0
OFFSET 0 mm
SET PEEL OFF
SET CUTTER OFF
SET PARTIAL_CUTTER OFF
SET TEAR ON
CLS
CODEPAGE 1252
; Lot (box) label. Built and sent by _print_lot_label() in test_console.py,
; to the printer Windows knows as LOTPRINTER. Two callers, one label:
;
;   Test Console -- OK on the "Lot quantity reached" dialog, for a box filled
;                   to the quantity the operator set for it.
;   Report page  -- PRINT BATCH LABEL, for a box left part-filled by a part
;                   change or a program close, with its quantity typed in.
;
; Both rebuild this file from scratch on every press, so each one is a fresh
; label carrying its own print time. Nothing is cached and nothing reprints.
;
; Every @name@ below is substituted before the file is sent, so this layout
; can be redrawn in the label designer without touching any Python. The full
; set of placeholders, all optional -- anything left out is simply not
; replaced, and anything with no value becomes an empty string:
;
;   @partNumber@   @modelName@   @alcCode@    @vendorCode@  @eoNumber@
;   @lotNo@        @lotQty@      @lotCount@   @empCode@
;   @machineID@    @machineID_NoAlphabet@
;   @ddMMyy@       @dd/MM/yy@    @HH:mm:ss@
;
; @lotQty@ is the box size and @lotCount@ is how many went into it. Both
; callers pass the same figure for the two -- a full box reached its quantity,
; and a short box is described by what it holds -- so the layout below draws
; QTY alone. They stayed separate fields because the count was once the day's
; running total, which made the second box of 50 read COUNT 100; it counts per
; box now, and a layout that wants it back has @lotCount@ waiting.
;
; Rotation 180 matches the part labels, which come off the roll the same way
; up. Under 180 the x below is the reading-LEFT edge of the line, so the
; shared x is what lines the block up down its left margin.
TEXT 265,172,"3",180,1,1,"LOT LABEL"
TEXT 265,140,"2",180,1,1,"P/NO  : @partNumber@"
TEXT 265,116,"2",180,1,1,"MODEL : @modelName@"
TEXT 265,92,"2",180,1,1,"QTY   : @lotQty@"
TEXT 265,68,"2",180,1,1,"LOT   : @lotNo@"
TEXT 265,44,"2",180,1,1,"DATE  : @dd/MM/yy@  @HH:mm:ss@"
TEXT 265,20,"2",180,1,1,"MC ID : @machineID@"
PRINT 1,1
